
	__init__.py					// imports+requires everything from funcs.hy (not touching macros.hy)
	lenses.hy					// stores only «import lenses [lens]», lns macros are in macros.hy
	strict.hy					// loads pydantic + some definitions like StrictInt

	/core   |
	        | from_hyrule.hy ↓	// some extracted funcs/macros from hyrule lib -> it loads much faster than hyrule
		    | funcs.hy		 •	// FINAL SOURCE OF TRUTH = Funcs defs here + Macros reimport (from: from_hyrule.hy and macros.hy)
		    | macros.hy	_____↑	// is allowed to depend only on from_hyrule.hy

	/monads |
	        | __init__.py		// monads may be imported all (import fptk.monads *) or one by one (import fptk.maybeM.hy)
		    | maybeM.hy
		    | resultM.hy

	·····························································································

	• why funcs.hy reimports macros and __init__ calls hy.eval(hyread(...)) on funcs.hy, but not on macros.hy?
      - because the aim is to have fast startup
      - if macros were in several places (like funcs.hy AND macros.hy AND from_hyrule.hy) this would require 3 expensive hy.eval calls

	• there is no /core.__init__.py to avoid extra hy.eval(hy.read...) call

	• lns macros are in macros.hy because:
	  - it saves 30ms load time (because we are avoiding to call extra hy.eval(hy.read...)) 
	  - to use lenses on top of fptk.core, you only need to call «import fptk.lenses *»

